    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1063">

                <pb facs="1215" n="1103" sameAs="frus:frus1935v03/pg1103"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">811.5034 (China) Thrift Corp./41: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in China</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Johnson</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Peiping</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1935-10-10T20:00:00+08:00">October 10, 1935—8
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received October 10—11:54 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>45. Embassy’s 42, October 10, 11 a.m. Following telegram has been received from
                    Judge of the United States Court for China.</p>
                <quote rend="blockquote">
                    <p>“I fully concur in proposed statement to be issued by Adams and request that
                        you instruct him to make it. With reference to the Department’s message to
                        you let me inform you that in a regular judicial proceeding in another case
                        several months ago this Court made a similar ruling and jurisdiction for
                        lack of substantial American interest but the case received no publicity. I
                        think the views of Governor of Nevada will not be helpful.”</p>
                </quote>
                <p>Embassy is instructing Adams to issue statement in question.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Johnson</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
